## Draw a layered neighbourhood diagram for a selected pattern
================================================================================

Context: The Patterns Discover page listed matching entities but did not show
what the pattern itself looks like. Selecting a pattern now draws a hop-layered
diagram (entity type, then neighbours at 1 / 2 / 3 hops) above the member list.
Hop expansion also keeps shortest-distance shells so the walk does not step
back onto nodes it already visited.

Changes:

1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py
   Materialise node types once; emit typed edges per hop; write
   `<out>_shape_edges`; skip already-seen nodes when expanding.
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern_diagram.py
   Pure builder: shape-edge rows + tokens → layered `{nodes, edges}`.
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobPatterns.py
   `/shape` can attach the diagram (opt-in, so materialize stays cheap).
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinAnalytics.py
   Pattern shape API requests the diagram.
5. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-patterns.js
   SVG diagram in Details; labels sit next to the target node.
6. src/front/static/simulation/css/simulation.css
   Diagram node / edge styles using theme variables.
7. tests/units/core/test_pattern_job_sql.py
   Typed edges, no backtrack to the anchor, shortest-distance shells.
8. tests/units/core/test_pattern_diagram.py
   Isolated pattern, hop/type nodes, attribute chips, edge cap.
9. tests/units/core/test_job_patterns.py
   Diagram is opt-in; missing edges table returns null.
10. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
    Details loads `/shape` and draws the diagram.
11. docs/user-guide.md, docs/architecture.md
    Diagram, `_shape_edges` table, `pattern_diagram.py`.

